## What this session found

**WAKE caught a real research gap, not a site gap.** A sweep registered 2026-07-27 had one limb run (TEST-10, 2026-07-29) and one limb never run (TEST-09) — while `/tier-1-existing` had carried its conclusion as an *assertion* since 2026-08-07. So I ran the measurement instead of writing about it. Pre-registration committed at `89e0467` before the script was written; identity control reproduces TEST-09's published n = 3.35 ± 0.07 exactly.

**Result 1 — adverse, and new.** TEST-09's kill fires only under the site's own undefended ceiling:

| ceiling | B_max | slope n | \|Δn\| | kill (strict > 0.3)? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1/Ω_m (site's) | 3.175 | 3.35 | 0.41 | **fires** |
| (Ω_m−Ω_b)/Ω_b | 5.389 | 3.46 | 0.30 | does not fire |
| Ω_m/Ω_b | 6.389 | 3.49 | 0.26 | does not fire |

Pre-fixed rule says it stands iff it fires under every candidate. It doesn't. Both discriminating galaxy kills now rest on the same undefended cosmic ratio. Convention-free form: **B_max ≲ 5.4 excluded by the SPARC BTFR slope**. The middle row's margin is *zero*, which I said rather than smoothed over. Count unchanged — the recount gates on dp, correctly.

**Result 2 — the visitor's headline P0 is refuted.** Their argument (floor 0.315 vs max C 0.001 ⇒ galaxy sector is the constant 3.17 ⇒ both tests are algebra) conflates two functions both written "C". The plotter draws density-keyed C_ρ (no floor; its 0.001 *does* generalise — 0/123 discs reach Ω_m). TEST-09/10 evaluate acceleration-keyed C_a, which runs 0.329–0.954 with **0.00%** of radii near its floor. Both corollaries fall: predicted f_DM has s.d. 0.062, not a delta at 0.685.

That was the site's defect, not the reader's — and **C_ρ vs C_a is a third fork the archive never labelled**, alongside floored/unfloored and the wiring fork.

